issues.body:
## Summary

Implement the first bounded learner used for SYS-01 and its matched control/attribution arms.

The student should remain intentionally small and inspectable. The scientific objective is to measure semantic-development accessibility under bounded resources, not to win a benchmark with architectural complexity.

## Scratch-training boundary

The student MUST inherit no task-capable pretrained neural weights.

"Scratch-trained" does **not** mean that every semantic token must start at an unrelated IID random coordinate. Initialization is an explicit experimental factor owned by #62.

The reference learner must support at least:

- `semantic_aligned` initialization for the integrated Bithkuil treatment;
- `iid_random` initialization for baseline and attribution controls;
- `semantic_permuted` initialization for alignment controls.

The student architecture remains fixed across these profiles. Initialization policy changes the initial parameter state, not the model topology.

## Initial architecture requirements

- fixed small architecture across representation arms;
- explicit initialization profile from #62;
- no inherited pretrained task-capable weights;
- four-answer supervised decoder at minimum: TRUE / FALSE / UNKNOWN / CONFLICT;
- deterministic initialization from explicit manifest/seed;
- fixed optimizer and schedule within each locked comparison;
- explicit parameter accounting including embeddings and output head;
- configurable context length and padding policy;
- activation/logit hooks for later diagnostics;
- backend-independent initialization loading so #64 can qualify Apple-Silicon acceleration.

## Reproducibility

Every run manifest must bind:

- architecture config;
- initialization profile and initializer manifest hash;
- semantic/token ABI hashes required by that profile;
- random seed where applicable;
- backend/device/runtime identity;
- precision policy;
- optimizer/schedule.

Two runs that claim the same student condition must not silently differ in initialization.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Architecture/config serialize to a stable machine-readable manifest.
- [ ] The same architecture can instantiate `semantic_aligned`, `iid_random`, and `semantic_permuted` through #62 without code-path-specific model topology.
- [ ] Same config/initializer manifest/seed reproduces initialization within declared numerical tolerance.
- [ ] No reference profile loads pretrained task-capable neural weights.
- [ ] Parameter counts and trainable-state sizes are emitted automatically.
- [ ] Initialization profile and tensor/manifest hashes are recorded automatically.
- [ ] Tiny overfit/smoke tests prove end-to-end gradient flow and answer decoding for the required profiles.
- [ ] Invalid outputs and calibration metrics are logged separately from accuracy.
- [ ] #42 can inspect the initialized embeddings before optimizer step one.
- [ ] The model can be moved to the #64 accelerated backend without silently regenerating or changing initialization.

## Non-goals

This issue does not:

- implement native BitNet/ternary training, which remains #19;
- decide whether semantic initialization helps, which is an empirical question;
- import pretrained embedding spaces into the student.

## Dependencies

#11 token ABI; #15 task endpoints; #62 semantic initialization.

Parent roadmap: #5.

## Publication posture

Public architecture/research specification.

